      "to": "miguel.alvarez@stateu.edu",
      "subject": "Guest lecture on agentic programming?",
      "message": "Hi Miguel,\n\nThank you for reaching out \u2014 we'd be delighted to have someone from the Jaseci team give a guest lecture on agentic programming for your graduate seminar. It's great to hear that your students have been experimenting with Jaseci already.\n\nWe have availability on both September 15 and September 22 at 2-4 pm Eastern, so either date works well for us. Please let us know which one you prefer, and we'll lock it in.\n\nFor the remote session, we'll need a video conferencing link (Zoom, Google Meet, or whichever platform your seminar uses). We'll handle the screen sharing for code demos. If you have any specific topics or areas within agentic programming you'd like us to focus on \u2014 for example, the Jac language, graph-based program structure (nodes, edges, walkers), or cloud deployment \u2014 just let us know and we'll tailor the talk accordingly.\n\nLooking forward to connecting with you and your students.\n\nBest regards,\nThe Jaseci Team\n"
    },
    {
      "to": "priya.nair@devfleet.io",
      "subject": "Quick question | byLLM structured output",
      "message": "Hi Priya,\n\nGreat question. Yes, byLLM supports structured outputs, so you won't need to parse the model's text manually.\n\nYou have a couple of options:\n\n1. **JSON mode** \u2014 Set the response format to JSON and provide a schema for the fields you want (severity, component, message). The model will return valid JSON conforming to your schema.\n\n2. **Typed outputs** \u2014 If you're using our SDK, you can define a Pydantic model or equivalent typed structure, and byLLM will return instances of that type directly.\n\nFor your log triage pipeline, I'd recommend defining a schema like:\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"severity\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"ERROR\", \"WARN\", \"INFO\", \"DEBUG\"]},\n    \"component\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n    \"message\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"severity\", \"component\", \"message\"]\n}\n```\n\nThis will give you clean, structured data you can feed directly into your pipeline without post-processing.\n\nIf you'd like a code sample or help integrating this into your workflow, just let me know.\n\nBest,\nbyLLM Team, Impact"
    }
  ],
